Z||000000||fierodude||06-22-2001||03:02 PM||||whats better the seats with the speakers built in or the newer ones that are on the panels? how do i get at the speakers in the seats? can you switch the bottoms of the seats onto a good pair of tops?<P>------------------<BR>slice the rice! it dosen't pay to drive jap - crap!||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-22-2001||04:28 PM||||ya, you can swap the tops and bottoms on all Fiero seats. Screws and Torx screws on both side hinges.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||06-22-2001||04:34 PM||||The seat cover on my '84 was one piece and to get at the speakers you would have to pull it off from the bottom up ( kinda like removing a ....condom . I like the speaker seats , but,  they are probably low-end in quality and the seat material must impede the sound somewhat. I also have a hole in my condom...I mean seatcover that I must repair.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT-maniac||06-22-2001||07:19 PM||||Well I have both types of seats in my fieros and I like the speakers in the headrests a lot better. I'm 5 ' 10 " and I find the speakers to be at the perfect height. Plus with those types of seats your getting 6 speaker stereo sound stock. Those seats do seem to be made of a cheaper fabric than the later ones and seem to wear more quickly. The later ones without speakers look nicer too with the added vinyl trim pieces and fiero logos. Don't know about replacing them as mine still sound great but I've heard it's not all that difficult try a search here.<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
